# =============================================================================
# EOS SDK third-party binaries
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These are staged from the SDK paths (sdkPath / sdkAndroidPath / sdkIosPath)
# by pre_build_step / post_build_step at build time, so they are NOT committed.
#
# The extension's OWN result binaries (EpicOnlineServices.dll, .dylib, and
# AndroidSource/libs/<abi>/libEpicOnlineServices.so) ARE committed and must stay
# tracked -- they are deliberately not matched below.
#
# Two zero-byte PLACEHOLDERS are also deliberately committed and must NOT be
# ignored here, or the reference they exist to create never reaches a clean
# checkout or the packaged asset:
#   libEOSSDK-Mac-Shipping.dylib        - declared as a Source File in the .yy so
#                                         the generated macOS Xcode project gets a
#                                         reference to it at compile time;
#                                         post_build_step overwrites the real one
#                                         into the OUTPUT folder, never here.
#   iOSSourceFromMac/EOSSDK.zip         - the asset compiler only picks up *.zip
#                                         from iOSSourceFromMac, so the entry has
#                                         to exist before pre_build_step fills it.
# pre_build_step DOES rewrite the iOS zip in place at build time, so expect it to
# show as modified after an iOS build - restore it rather than committing the SDK.
# Same arrangement as GMEXT-Discord's libdiscord_partner_sdk.dylib /
# discord_partner_sdk.zip placeholders.
# =============================================================================

# Android (EOS SDK) -- staged as a whole AAR, consumed directly by Gradle
/AndroidSource/libs-aar/*.aar

# iOS staging temp (EOS xcframework, signature-stripped before zipping)
/_eos_xcfw_tmp/
# iOS raw xcframework staged on Windows for remote_build_step.sh (transient)
/iOSSourceFromMac/EOSSDK.xcframework/

# Windows / Linux (EOS C SDK runtime libs). macOS's libEOSSDK-Mac-Shipping.dylib
# at this same level is the committed placeholder described above - not ignored.
/EOSSDK-Win64-Shipping.dll
/EOSSDK-Win32-Shipping.dll
/libEOSSDK-Linux-Shipping.so
